  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an owner who wants **brand affiliation without losing individuality**, the strongest options in the Caribbean and Latin America are usually the **soft brands** and **collection brands** from Hilton, IHG, Hyatt, and Marriott, with Accor and Radisson also offering relevant collection-style choices in the region.[4][6][7][5]\n\nThe most relevant brands to consider are:\n\n- **Hilton**: **Curio Collection by Hilton**, **Tapestry Collection by Hilton**, and **Vignette Collection** are explicitly used in CALA for independent or distinctive hotels, and Hilton has continued expanding these flags across the region.[6][7]\n- **IHG**: **Vignette Collection** and **Voco** are the clearest fit if the goal is preserving a hotel’s identity while gaining a global distribution and loyalty platform; IHG describes Voco as giving owners recognition without having to create a new hotel identity.[4]\n- **Hyatt**: **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt** is the main soft/collection-style option for distinctive properties, while Hyatt’s broader **Inclusive Collection** is also highly relevant in the Caribbean and Latin America for resort owners, though it is more standardized than a classic soft brand.[2][3]\n- **Marriott**: **Autograph Collection**, **Tribute Portfolio**, and **The Luxury Collection** are the key soft/collection brands for independent-style positioning, especially for upscale and luxury assets in resort destinations.[3]\n- **Accor**: **MGallery** and **Emblems** are the most relevant collection-style options for owners seeking a more distinctive, locally rooted hotel identity in the region.[3]\n- **Radisson/Choice-related platform**: **Radisson Individuals** and **Ascend Collection** are relevant if the property wants a lighter-touch affiliation with strong branding flexibility in LATAM and the Caribbean.[5]\n\nIf you want the **best starting shortlist**, it would be:\n\n- **Hilton Curio / Tapestry / Vignette**\n- **IHG Vignette / Voco**\n- **Marriott Autograph / Tribute**\n- **Hyatt Unbound Collection**\n- **Accor MGallery**\n- **Radisson Individuals / Ascend Collection**[4][6][7][5]\n\nFor the Caribbean and Latin America specifically, these brands are attractive because the region has seen strong growth in **all-inclusives, branded residences, and conversion-friendly soft brands**, and owners are often looking for global distribution while keeping local character intact.[1][2][4]\n\nIf you want, I can also narrow this down by **hotel type**: luxury resort, lifestyle boutique, all-inclusive, or conversion asset.",
